# =============================================================================
# Global .gitignore — SplendidCube workspace
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source of truth: the `common-files` repo. `dev-env` syncs this file into every
# project root and refreshes it on each update, so DO NOT edit it inside a
# project — change it here in `common-files` instead.
#
# For ignores that are specific to one project and should NOT be shared, use
# `.git/info/exclude` (untracked, local to that clone) rather than editing the
# synced copy.
#
# Covers: macOS / Windows / Linux, editors & IDEs, Rust, Node/Bun/Nuxt 4/Vue 3,
# TypeScript, Swift/Xcode (native macOS desktop apps), JVM/Gradle plugins, Python
# tooling, secrets, logs & temp files.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.TemporaryItems
.VolumeIcon.icns
Icon?

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# Linux
*~
.directory
.Trash-*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors & IDEs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JetBrains (local IDE state; shared run configs are managed separately)
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# VS Code (shared settings are synced via common-files; drop only local noise)
.history/
*.code-workspace
.vscode/*.local

# Vim / Emacs / misc backups
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.\#*
\#*\#
*.bak
*.orig

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust  (apps, CLIs, AWS Lambda, models, postgres-engine, core)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# NOTE: Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — most repos here are
# binaries / Lambdas, which commit their lockfile for reproducible builds.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / Bun / Nuxt 4 / Vue 3  (web, weblib, i18n)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.nuxt/
.output/
.nitro/
.data/
# No trailing slash: some web repos expose `dist` as a symlink to the Nuxt
# static output (`dist -> .output/public`) for hosts that publish from `dist/`.
# `dist/` would only match a real directory and let that symlink slip through.
dist
.cache/
.vite/
.temp/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
# NOTE: bun.lockb is intentionally NOT ignored — commit it for reproducible installs.

# Playwright E2E (saved auth state, reports, failure artefacts)
/e2e/.auth/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Swift / Xcode / SwiftPM  (native macOS desktop apps — macos-desktop-app)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/
DerivedData/
.build-xcode/
.swiftpm/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout
*.xcodeproj/
*.generated.plist
*.generated.entitlements
# Vendored-C build scratch: build-libgit2.sh (and any sibling vendor builds) stage
# sources, build trees, and install roots here — hundreds of MB; only the finished
# .xcframework under Vendor/ is committed.
.libgit2-build/
# Test-result / archive / symbol bundles and coverage droppings from xcodebuild and
# `swift test` runs that land outside the ignored derived-data dirs.
*.xcresult/
*.xcarchive/
*.dSYM/
*.profraw
*.profdata
# NOTE: Package.resolved is intentionally NOT ignored — commit it for reproducible
# dependency resolution (like Cargo.lock / bun.lockb above).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JVM / Gradle  (JetBrains plugin archetype)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
out/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python  (bootstrap / tooling scripts)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment & secrets
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.local
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs & temporary files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
bun-debug.log*
*.tmp
*.temp
tmp/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local script cache  (managed by the shared makefile)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `run-script` (in ~/.splendidcube/makefile.mk) downloads makefile scripts into
# scripts/<technology>/ on demand. The folder is kept (.gitkeep) but everything
# downloaded into it is transient — never commit it.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/.gitkeep

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared suite libraries  (symlinked in by `dev-env`)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `dev-env` (setup/projects.yaml) links the shared lib checkouts a repo consumes
# into `<repo>/libs/` — cloud apps get cloudlib + weblib, web apps get weblib —
# so dev containers can bind-mount them at /cloudlib and /weblib.
#
# One rule for the whole directory, not one per library: a rule per library meant
# every new shared lib needed a change here, and any repo still on a stale copy
# of this file silently started tracking the new link. `libs/` is a real
# directory (the links are inside it), so the trailing slash is correct.
/libs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Synced project config  (installed fresh on every `make update`)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `scripts/common/update-files.sh` re-installs these from the common-files / ai
# repos on each update, so the synced copy is the source of truth —
# committing them would only let a stale copy drift. The committed exceptions are
# this .gitignore and scripts/.gitkeep (which ARE tracked).
#
# EXCEPTION — per-project AI files are render-once and PROJECT-OWNED, so they are
# tracked & committed (NOT synced over): CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md,
# .github/copilot-instructions.md, and .claude/project.manifest. `update-ai.sh`
# renders these once from the `ai` templates and never overwrites them. Everything
# else under .claude/ (rules, settings.json, agents/commands/hooks, VERSION) stays
# synced from the `ai` repo and out of version control.

# AI assistant config — from the `ai` repo.
# Ignore all of .claude/ EXCEPT the per-project manifest (git can't re-include a
# file whose parent dir is excluded, so glob the children and negate the manifest).
/.claude/*
!/.claude/project.manifest
# Per-developer local Claude overrides (never synced, never committed)
CLAUDE.local.md
# NOTE: AGENTS.md and /.github/copilot-instructions.md are intentionally NOT ignored
# — they are per-project, render-once, and committed (see the EXCEPTION above).

# Dev container — GENERATED by `dev-env`, never synced and never committed.
#
# dev-env writes a .devcontainer/ at every hierarchy level and every repo: a small
# generated compose wrapper plus symlinks into the `devcontainer` repo's template
# tree. This ignore rule is what makes that safe — it is the single mechanism
# stopping a level's copy from being committed and drifting away from the template
# it was rendered from. dev-env refuses to deploy into a repo where this rule is
# missing rather than create committable content, so keep it.
/.devcontainer/

# Standard root configs — from the `common-files` repo (add new ones here as they
# are introduced, so the synced copy stays out of version control)
/.editorconfig
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/rust-toolchain.toml
/rustfmt.toml
/deny.toml
/biome.json
/eslint.config.mjs
/.swiftlint.yml
/.swift-format
